    description: "STATEMENT: a second call from one caller to one target is not reported as an unresolved call. OBSERVED: inherited_calls, receiver_type_dispatch and single_holder_name keep one edge per (caller, target) and leave the later stubs open (call_lines are collapsed on the first). Consumers that count unresolved edges, and the pilot's own lost lists, read them as unknown (JS/TS L3 of the second round; 3 Rust artifacts). The name step had to re-derive 'answered' from the imports for this reason (e948d2ae3).\n\nEvidence and method: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/pilot_11252026/DESIGN.md and final/ (maps mine_e948 at e948d2ae3 against before/ at dev 0d3c12ff4; hand samples seed 20261125). Found during the ADR-0064 pilot (rust, csharp, javascript/typescript); not built there because fewer than two of the three pilot languages need it, or because it is the analyzer's own."  # a121
